ne  you kind of cook it you glaze it you  know you cook it normally as you would  [Music]  and the trickiest part is transferring  that slab of beautiful glazed meat onto  a nice bun and the key here is to  actually get a nice piece of toasted  bread that matches whatever the ribs  you're going to make so as long as you  get some bread and you toast it and you  butter it and it fits with the rib  [Music]  and you kind of add you know you can add  whatever toppings you want i  i like onions so i chose to add onions  and some parsley  [Music]  the coolest part is when you actually  serve it because when you slice it along  the edges of the sandwich you're  actually going to get one rib per person  and it's because like that's like one  sandwich per person  so you just cut it up into what you  think where the ribs were everybody gets  a nice sandwich that they can just chomp  on and it's you know it's like a  boneless rib and what could be better  than that i was surprised it actually  turned out really well it's kind of like  your childhood uh you know fast food rib  sandwich reimagined with actual ribs  because who knows what's in the original  one  but that's pretty much it and i think  this is a great recipe if you  want to have friends over it's great for  potlucks it's great for parties you know  i think you can pretty much blow  people's minds and if you know you do  make it tag me send it over i i love i  love when uh i think it's awesome when  you guys make our recipes so i think  that's a keeper for sure if you want to  entertain if you just want some ribs or  if you're just looking for lunch like me  on a weekly basis  you
 

